<p>This Privacy Policy explains how personal data is processed when you use this website, in accordance with the General Data Protection Regulation (EU) 2016/679 ("GDPR", in Polish "RODO") and Polish data protection law.</p>

<h2>1. Data controller</h2>
<p>The controller of your personal data is <strong>{{ $mosqueName }}</strong>@if($mosqueAddress), {{ $mosqueAddress }}@endif. @if($mosqueEmail)You can contact us about any data protection matter at <a href="mailto:{{ $mosqueEmail }}">{{ $mosqueEmail }}</a>.@endif</p>

<h2>2. What data we process, why, and on what legal basis</h2>
<h3>a) Visiting the website</h3>
<p>When you visit the website, our server automatically processes technical data such as your IP address, browser type, date and time of access and the pages requested. This is necessary to deliver the website securely and to prevent abuse. Legal basis: our legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).</p>

<h3>b) Contact form and e-mail</h3>
<p>When you contact us via the form or by e-mail, we process your name, e-mail address, optional phone number, subject and message in order to answer your enquiry. Legal basis: steps taken at your request (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR) and our legitimate interest in responding to correspondence (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). Please do not include sensitive information (for example about health or religious beliefs) unless it is necessary for your enquiry; if you do, you consent to its processing for that purpose (Art. 9(2)(a) GDPR).</p>

<h3>c) Analytics (only with your consent)</h3>
<p>If you accept analytics cookies, we use Google Analytics 4 (Google Ireland Limited, Gordon House, Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland) to produce aggregated statistics about how the website is used. Legal basis: your consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR and Art. 399 of the Polish Electronic Communications Law). Google may transfer data to the USA; such transfers are based on the EU–US Data Privacy Framework and/or Standard Contractual Clauses. Analytics is not loaded until you give consent.</p>

<h3>d) External media (only with your consent)</h3>
<p>Videos (YouTube, Vimeo, Facebook) and maps (Google Maps) are only loaded after you allow "External media". The respective provider then receives your IP address and may set its own cookies. Legal basis: your consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR).</p>

<h3>e) Fonts</h3>
<p>The website loads fonts from Google Fonts. To deliver them, your browser connects to Google servers, which receive your IP address. Legal basis: our legitimate interest in a consistent presentation of the website (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).</p>

<h2>3. Recipients</h2>
<p>Your data may be disclosed to service providers acting on our behalf (hosting, e-mail and IT services) under data processing agreements, to the providers named above where you have given consent, and to public authorities where required by law. We do not sell personal data.</p>

<h2>4. How long we keep data</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Server logs: for a short period necessary for security, usually no longer than 30 days.</li>
    <li>Contact enquiries: for as long as needed to handle your enquiry and any follow-up, and then deleted, unless the law requires longer retention.</li>
    <li>Consent records: for as long as the consent cookie is valid (6 months) or until you change your choice.</li>
    <li>Analytics cookies: see the <a href="{{ route('legal.cookies') }}">Cookie Policy</a>.</li>
</ul>

<h2>5. Your rights</h2>
<p>You have the right to access your data, to rectification, erasure, restriction of processing, data portability, and to object to processing based on legitimate interest. Where processing is based on consent, you may withdraw it at any time without affecting the lawfulness of processing before withdrawal, for cookies via the "Cookie settings" link at the bottom of every page.</p>
<p>You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the supervisory authority: the President of the Personal Data Protection Office (Prezes Urzędu Ochrony Danych Osobowych), ul. Stawki 2, 00-193 Warszawa, <a href="https://uodo.gov.pl" target="_blank" rel="noopener">uodo.gov.pl</a>.</p>

<h2>6. Voluntary provision of data</h2>
<p>Providing data is voluntary. Without the data required in the contact form we cannot reply to your enquiry. We do not use automated decision-making or profiling.</p>

<h2>7. Changes</h2>
<p>We may update this policy when our services or the law change. The current version is always available on this page.</p>
